\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The controlled Gaussian depth sweep with the host (Qwen3-1.7B) and the removed direction $r$ held fixed. Completion never varies: the peak layer is annihilated to $\log _{10}\min _W e_W(r) = -4.53$ at every spread. What varies is discovery. Between spread 8 and 16 the kernel's minimum depth weight rises from 0.0796 to 0.5311, $|\cos (v_1,r)|$ jumps from 0.126 to 0.9992, and $W05$ falls from the parent's $-1.0098$ to $-2.888$, crossing the operating threshold. Below that transition the pooled statistic returns the parent's value to four decimals however complete the edit.}}{10}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:fig4}{{2}{10}{The controlled Gaussian depth sweep with the host (Qwen3-1.7B) and the removed direction $r$ held fixed. Completion never varies: the peak layer is annihilated to $\log _{10}\min _W e_W(r) = -4.53$ at every spread. What varies is discovery. Between spread 8 and 16 the kernel's minimum depth weight rises from 0.0796 to 0.5311, $|\cos (v_1,r)|$ jumps from 0.126 to 0.9992, and $W05$ falls from the parent's $-1.0098$ to $-2.888$, crossing the operating threshold. Below that transition the pooled statistic returns the parent's value to four decimals however complete the edit}{figure.2}{}}
